1
00:00:10,130 --> 00:00:15,130
This is the first video presentation for the Case Animal and Plant Biotechnology course.

2
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:19,130
As you view this video, be sure to make notes of important information.

3
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:24,130
Feel free to pause, repeat, and resume the video whenever necessary.

4
00:00:24,130 --> 00:00:31,130
Safety in the Biotechnology Laboratory Lesson 1.2, Standard Operating Procedures

5
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:35,130
You completed Lesson 1.1, Foundations of Biotechnology,

6
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:41,130
during which you got a good idea of the breadth and depth of the biotechnology field.

7
00:00:41,130 --> 00:00:44,130
In all laboratories, safety is a priority.

8
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:51,130
In the Biotechnology Lab, safety may be of greater concern due to the biological hazards.

9
00:00:51,130 --> 00:00:54,130
There are many definitions for safety.

10
00:00:54,130 --> 00:00:57,130
Most simply put, safety is the freedom from accidents.

11
00:00:57,130 --> 00:01:03,170
Safety is a personal responsibility.

12
00:01:03,170 --> 00:01:06,170
The person most responsible for your safety is you.

13
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:10,170
You are also responsible for respecting the safety of others

14
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:16,170
and acting in a manner that is safe for you, your classmates, and school property.

15
00:01:16,170 --> 00:01:23,170
Having an attitude of safety is the first step to being responsible and respectful in the laboratory.

16
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:28,170
A safe attitude includes positive commitment to behaving responsibly.

17
00:01:28,170 --> 00:01:34,280
Personal protective equipment should be worn at all times in the laboratory

18
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:39,280
to minimize injuries and damage as well as to avoid contamination of research.

19
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:49,900
Throughout this course, you will be expected to choose and utilize appropriate PPE for all laboratory activity.

20
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:58,900
Working in the laboratory will help you understand many of the complex processes involved with agriculture and natural resource research.

21
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:05,900
However, there are hazards present when working with glass, chemicals, fire, and tools.

22
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:09,900
Always use materials as instructed with care.

23
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:13,900
Most accidents can be avoided by following procedures and acting cautiously.

24
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:22,620
Always consider the nature of the item you are disposing of and review proper disposal techniques.

25
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:27,620
Your teacher will provide specific, local instructions as necessary.

26
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:36,300
Review systems for cleaning glassware and other materials in your situation.

27
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:41,300
Disinfection and sterilization techniques are critical in biotechnology research.

28
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:48,900
Accidents happen in labs. Solutions get spilled and glass gets broken.

29
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:54,900
Due to the nature of chemicals used, please report all spills and broken items to your teacher.

30
00:02:54,900 --> 00:03:00,980
Work together to clean up properly and safely.

31
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:04,980
The lab facility is equipped with spill kits and equipment.

32
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:11,310
You will review the locations and use of these items in this lesson.

33
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:19,310
In research, procedures and protocols must be carefully documented in order to repeat experiments and even pursue future patents.

34
00:03:19,310 --> 00:03:26,310
Notebooks may be used to identify potential unsafe reactions or errors in procedures that led to accidents.

35
00:03:26,310 --> 00:03:31,490
Be sure to record everything accurately.

36
00:03:31,490 --> 00:03:38,490
When recording data, it is helpful to use charts, graphs, tables, pictures, or any combinations of those.

37
00:03:38,490 --> 00:03:44,490
Refer to the Laboratory Notebook Guidelines document for your textbook when questions arise.

38
00:03:44,490 --> 00:03:53,050
As a review, marker highlight three key points in your notes that are important to remember from this presentation.

39
00:03:53,050 --> 00:03:57,050
List two ideas or concepts that relate to previous knowledge.

40
00:03:57,050 --> 00:04:00,050
List any questions you have about this topic.

41
00:04:00,050 --> 00:04:03,050
Discuss these questions with your instructor.

42
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:09,050
Keep any notes you have from this presentation organized and available for use throughout the course.

43
00:04:09,050 --> 00:04:16,050
Through activity 121, Surrounded by Safety, you will determine safe practices, identify safety equipment,

44
00:04:16,050 --> 00:04:21,050
and explain how to use safety equipment appropriately in the biotechnology laboratory.

45
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:28,050
Diligence and following safety procedures and rules will improve your professional success during research.

46
00:04:28,050 --> 00:04:30,050
Your teacher will provide more instructions.
